    "content": {
      "value": "This page documents the end-to-end MuleSoft → SFCC synchronisation process for three data domains: **Product**, **Price**, and **Inventory**. All three domains share the same WebDAV-based delivery mechanism and SFCC import job pattern.\n\nRelated pages: - TSD: Product — SFCC Catalogue & Data Integration - TSD: Product — SFCC Product Attributes - TSD: Price — SFCC Pricebooks & Global-e - TSD: Inventory — SFCC ↔ MuleSoft ↔ NewStore / AP21\n\n---\n\n1-overview1. Overview\n---------------------\n\nAP21 is the system of record for product and price data. NewStore is the system of record for inventory availability. MuleSoft is the integration layer for all three — SFCC never connects to AP21 or NewStore directly.\n\nAll three sync domains use the same delivery pattern:\n\n1. MuleSoft generates a domain-specific SFCC-compliant XML zip\n2. MuleSoft uploads the zip to SFCC via **WebDAV** (overwriting a fixed filename in the `incoming/` folder)\n3. MuleSoft triggers the SFCC import job via the **SCAPI Jobs Admin API**\n4. MuleSoft polls for job completion\n5. On success — zip is archived with a timestamp; on failure — zip is moved to a failed folder and an alert is raised\n\n> **API Note:** OCAPI is deprecated. All job trigger and status poll calls use the **SCAPI Jobs Admin API** ([reference](https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/commerce/commerce-api/references/jobs)). Authentication uses **Account Manager OAuth2 (AmOAuth2)** — not OCAPI Client ID/Secret.\n\n| Domain | Source | MuleSoft API | SFCC Import Job | Frequency |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Product | AP21 | product-prc-api | `sfcc-site-archive-import` | Event-driven (AP21 product create/update) + scheduled batch — TBC |\n| Price | AP21 | product-prc-api (price feed) | `sfcc-site-archive-import` | Scheduled — full or delta — TBC |\n| Inventory | NewStore | `inventory-sync-prc-api` | `sfcc-site-archive-import` | Every 15 minutes |\n\n---\n\n2-webdav-folder-structure2. WebDAV Folder Structure\n---------------------------------------------------\n\nSFCC exposes a WebDAV endpoint for file-based integration. MuleSoft authenticates to WebDAV using **Account Manager OAuth2 (AmOAuth2)** — the same token used for SCAPI Admin API calls.\n\n**Base path:**\n\nnonewide760https://{instance}.commercecloud.salesforce.com\n/on/demandware.servlet/webdav/Sites/Impex/src/instance/\n\n**Folder layout — one set per domain:**\n\nnonewide760/Impex/src/instance/\n├── product/\n│ ├── incoming/\n│ │ └── catalog-import.zip ← fixed filename, overwritten each run\n│ ├── archive/\n│ │ ├── catalog-import-20250709-143022.zip\n│ │ └── catalog-import-20250708-060012.zip\n│ └── failed/\n│ └── catalog-import-20250707-183045.zip\n│\n├── price/\n│ ├── incoming/\n│ │ └── pricebook-import.zip ← fixed filename, overwritten each run\n│ ├── archive/\n│ └── failed/\n│\n└── inventory/\n├── incoming/\n│ └── inventory-import.zip ← fixed filename, overwritten each run\n├── archive/\n└── failed/\n\n**Fixed filename rationale:** MuleSoft always writes the same filename to `incoming/`, overwriting the previous file. The timestamp is applied only at archive time (move from `incoming/` → `archive/` or `failed/`). This keeps the SFCC job configuration static — no dynamic file path parameter is required per execution.\n\n---\n\n3-sync-orchestration--mulesoft-flow-all-domains3. Sync Orchestration — MuleSoft Flow (All Domains)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nThe following sequence applies to all three domains. Domain-specific variations are noted in Sections 4, 5, and 6.\n\n**SCAPI Jobs Admin API base URL:**\n\nnonewide760https://{shortCode}.api.commercecloud.salesforce.com/jobs/v1/organizations/{organizationId}\n\n**Auth:**`Authorization: Bearer {amOAuth2Token}` — token obtained from Account Manager using client credentials grant.\n\nnonewide760AP21 / NewStore (source event or scheduler trigger)\n│\n▼\nMuleSoft\n│\n├── 1. GUARD CHECK\n│ GET /jobs/v1/organizations/{organizationId}/jobs/{jobId}/executions\n│ ?status=Running\n│ If a previous execution is running → hold; retry after interval\n│ If clear → proceed\n│\n├── 2. GENERATE XML ZIP\n│ Transform source payload → SFCC-compliant XML\n│ Package as zip (see domain sections for zip contents)\n│\n├── 3. WEBDAV UPLOAD (overwrite)\n│ PUT https://{instance}.commercecloud.salesforce.com\n│ /on/demandware.servlet/webdav/Sites/Impex/src/instance/\n│ {domain}/incoming/{fixed-filename}.zip\n│ Overwrites any previously uploaded file\n│\n├── 4. TRIGGER IMPORT JOB (SCAPI Jobs Admin API)\n│ POST /jobs/v1/organizations/{organizationId}/jobs/sfcc-site-archive-import/executions\n│ Headers: Authorization: Bearer {amOAuth2Token}\n│ Body:\n│ {\n│ \"parameters\": [\n│ { \"name\": \"ImportFile\", \"value\": \"{domain}/incoming/{fixed-filename}.zip\" },\n│ { \"name\": \"ImportMode\", \"value\": \"merge\" }\n│ ]\n│ }\n│ → returns { \"id\": \"{executionId}\", \"executionStatus\": \"pending\" }\n│\n├── 5. POLL JOB STATUS\n│ GET /jobs/v1/organizations/{organizationId}/jobs/sfcc-site-archive-import/executions/{executionId}\n│ Poll every 10 seconds until executionStatus ≠ \"running\"\n│\n├── 6a. ON executionStatus: \"finished\" (exitStatus: \"ok\")\n│ ├── Fetch BM import log from WebDAV /Impex/log/ — check for per-record errors\n│ └── WebDAV MOVE {domain}/incoming/{fixed-filename}.zip\n│ → {domain}/archive/{fixed-filename}-{YYYYMMDD-HHmmss}.zip\n│\n└── 6b. ON executionStatus: \"finished\" (exitStatus: \"error\") OR \"failed\"\n├── WebDAV MOVE {domain}/incoming/{fixed-filename}.zip\n│ → {domain}/failed/{fixed-filename}-{YYYYMMDD-HHmmss}.zip\n└── Raise alert — Anypoint monitoring notification\n> **Note:** SFCC does not move or clean up files on WebDAV after import. MuleSoft owns the full lifecycle — upload, trigger, archive, and cleanup.\n\n---\n\n4-product-sync4. Product Sync\n-----------------------------\n\n### 41-trigger4.1 Trigger\n\nAP21 product create or update event consumed by MuleSoft, or a scheduled full/delta batch. Trigger pattern to be confirmed with MuleSoft team — see open item #1.\n\n### 42-zip-contents4.2 Zip Contents\n\nProduct sync delivers **catalog XML only**. Pricebook XML is always delivered separately via the price sync (Section 5) — including during initial load. Both syncs run independently on their own schedules and WebDAV paths.\n\nnonewide760catalog-import.zip\n└── catalogs/\n└── zimmermann-catalog/\n└── catalog.xml ← master products, variants, attributes, category assignments\n\n### 43-catalogxml-structure4.3 catalog.xml Structure\n\nMuleSoft generates one catalog XML per run covering all sites. Multi-locale content uses `xml:lang` attributes per the locale table in TSD: Product — SFCC Catalogue & Data Integration.\n\nxmlwide760<catalog xmlns=\"http://www.demandware.com/xml/impex/catalog/2006-10-31\"\ncatalog-id=\"zimmermann-catalog\">\n<!-- Master product -->\n<product product-id=\"4673TS251\">\n<display-name xml:lang=\"x-default\">Aster Fit &amp; Flare Dress</display-name>\n<long-description xml:lang=\"x-default\">...</long-description>\n<online-flag>true</online-flag>\n<searchable-flag>true</searchable-flag>\n<tax-class-id>standard</tax-class-id>\n<custom-attributes>\n<custom-attribute attribute-id=\"styleNumber\">4673TS251</custom-attribute>\n<custom-attribute attribute-id=\"season\">SS25</custom-attribute>\n<custom-attribute attribute-id=\"label\">Ready to Wear</custom-attribute>\n<custom-attribute attribute-id=\"fabricComposition\">100% Silk</custom-attribute>\n<custom-attribute attribute-id=\"careInstructions\">Dry clean only</custom-attribute>\n<custom-attribute attribute-id=\"countryOfOrigin\">China</custom-attribute>\n<custom-attribute attribute-id=\"isFinalSale\">false</custom-attribute>\n</custom-attributes>\n<variations>\n<attributes>\n<variation-attribute attribute-id=\"color\" variation-attribute-id=\"color\">\n<variation-attribute-values>\n<variation-attribute-value value=\"GVSCP\">\n<display-value xml:lang=\"x-default\">Guava Seascape</display-value>\n</variation-attribute-value>\n</variation-attribute-values>\n</variation-attribute>\n<variation-attribute attribute-id=\"size\" variation-attribute-id=\"size\"/>\n</attributes>\n<variants>\n<variant product-id=\"4673TS251GVSCP0P\"/>\n</variants>\n</variations>\n</product>\n<!-- Variant product -->\n<product product-id=\"4673TS251GVSCP0P\">\n<upc>9312345678901</upc>\n<online-flag>true</online-flag>\n<searchable-flag>false</searchable-flag>\n<custom-attributes>\n<custom-attribute attribute-id=\"color\">GVSCP</custom-attribute>\n<custom-attribute attribute-id=\"refinementColor\">Guava Seascape</custom-attribute>\n<custom-attribute attribute-id=\"size\">0P</custom-attribute>\n</custom-attributes>\n</product>\n</catalog>\n\n### 44-import-mode4.4 Import Mode\n\nThe catalog XML must use **merge mode** — not replace. This prevents unintended deletion of products not included in a delta feed.\n\nxmlwide760<catalog xmlns=\"...\" catalog-id=\"zimmermann-catalog\">\n<!-- mode=\"merge\" is the default for catalog import — do not use mode=\"replace\" for delta feeds -->\n\n---\n\n5-price-sync5. Price Sync\n-------------------------\n\n### 51-trigger5.1 Trigger\n\nScheduled — full reload or delta on price change. Runs independently from the product sync on its own schedule. Frequency and delta vs full strategy to be confirmed — see open item #2.\n\n### 52-zip-contents5.2 Zip Contents\n\nPrice sync delivers **pricebook XML for domestic sites only**. International sites (USIntl, EUIntl, HK, ME) are served by **Global-e** which handles all currency conversion and pricing at checkout — SFCC does not hold per-currency pricebooks for those sites.\n\nAll pricebook XML files are placed inside a `pricebooks/` folder so the `sfcc-site-archive-import` job correctly identifies and processes them.\n\nnonewide760pricebook-import.zip\n└── pricebooks/\n├── au-aud-list-prices.xml ← ZimmermannAU\n├── au-aud-sale-prices.xml\n├── uk-gbp-list-prices.xml ← ZimmermannUK\n├── uk-gbp-sale-prices.xml\n├── us-usd-list-prices.xml ← ZimmermannUS (domestic)\n├── us-usd-sale-prices.xml\n├── eu-eur-list-prices.xml ← ZimmermannEU\n└── eu-eur-sale-prices.xml\n\n**Total: 8 pricebook XML files per sync run** — list + sale for AU, UK, US, EU.\n\n| Site | Pricebooks in sync | Currency managed by |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ZimmermannAU | `au-aud-list-prices`, `au-aud-sale-prices` | SFCC (AP21 via MuleSoft) |\n| ZimmermannUK | `uk-gbp-list-prices`, `uk-gbp-sale-prices` | SFCC (AP21 via MuleSoft) |\n| ZimmermannUS | `us-usd-list-prices`, `us-usd-sale-prices` | SFCC (AP21 via MuleSoft) |\n| ZimmermannEU | `eu-eur-list-prices`, `eu-eur-sale-prices` | SFCC (AP21 via MuleSoft) |\n| ZimmermannUSIntl | — | Global-e |\n| ZimmermannEUIntl | — | Global-e |\n| ZimmermannHK | — | Global-e |\n| ZimmermannME | — | Global-e |\n\nFull pricebook register for all sites: TSD: Price — SFCC Pricebooks & Global-e\n\n### 53-pricebook-xml-structure5.3 Pricebook XML Structure\n\nxmlwide760<pricebook xmlns=\"http://www.demandware.com/xml/impex/pricebook/2006-10-31\"\npricebook-id=\"au-aud-list-prices\">\n<header>\n<currency>AUD</currency>\n<display-name xml:lang=\"x-default\">AU List Prices</display-name>\n<online-flag>true</online-flag>\n</header>\n<price-tables>\n<price-table product-id=\"4673TS251GVSCP0P\">\n<amount quantity=\"1\">895.00</amount>\n</price-table>\n</price-tables>\n</pricebook>\n\nSale pricebooks reference their parent list pricebook:\n\nxmlwide760<pricebook pricebook-id=\"au-aud-sale-prices\">\n<header>\n<currency>AUD</currency>\n<parent>au-aud-list-prices</parent>\n<online-flag>true</online-flag>\n</header>\n<price-tables>\n<price-table product-id=\"4673TS251GVSCP0P\">\n<amount quantity=\"1\">595.00</amount>\n</price-table>\n</price-tables>\n</pricebook>\n\n### 54-price-on-variant-only5.4 Price on Variant Only\n\nPrices are set on **variant** products only — never on master products. SFCC resolves the effective price by checking the sale pricebook first, then falling back to the list pricebook.\n\n---\n\n6-inventory-sync6. Inventory Sync\n---------------------------------\n\n### 61-trigger6.1 Trigger\n\nMuleSoft `inventory-sync-prc-api` runs every 15 minutes per region (AU, GB, US). EU, EUIntl, HK, ME coverage to be confirmed — see open item #3.\n\n### 62-source6.2 Source\n\nNewStore — availability export via S3 compressed file per fulfilment group. MuleSoft downloads, decompresses, transforms to SFCC inventory XML, and delivers via WebDAV.\n\nFull NewStore → MuleSoft detail: TSD: Inventory — SFCC ↔ MuleSoft ↔ NewStore / AP21\n\n### 63-zip-contents6.3 Zip Contents\n\nnonewide760inventory-import.zip\n└── inventory-lists/\n└── inventory.xml ← all per-site inventory list records in one file\n\n### 64-inventory-xml-structure6.4 Inventory XML Structure\n\nxmlwide760<inventory xmlns=\"http://www.demandware.com/xml/impex/inventory/2006-10-31\">\n<inventory-list>\n<header list-id=\"inventory\\_m\\_au\">\n<default-instock>false</default-instock>\n<description>AU Inventory</description>\n</header>\n<records>\n<record product-id=\"4673TS251GVSCP0P\"\nquantity=\"12\"\nallocation=\"12\"\nperpetual=\"false\"/>\n</records>\n</inventory-list>\n</inventory>\n\n### 65-persite-inventory-lists6.5 Per-Site Inventory Lists\n\n| Site | Inventory List ID | Sync Region |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ZimmermannAU | `inventory_m_au` | AU |\n| ZimmermannUK | `inventory_m_uk` | GB |\n| ZimmermannUS | `inventory_m_us` | US |\n| ZimmermannUSIntl | `inventory_m_us` | US (shared pool) |\n| ZimmermannEU | `inventory_m_eu` | TBC |\n| ZimmermannEUIntl | `inventory_m_eu_intl` | TBC |\n| ZimmermannHK | `inventory_m_hk` | TBC |\n| ZimmermannME | `inventory_m_me` | TBC |\n\n---\n\n7-webdav-archive-strategy7. WebDAV Archive Strategy\n---------------------------------------------------\n\n| Behaviour | Detail |\n| --- | --- |\n| Incoming filename | Fixed — `catalog-import.zip` / `pricebook-import.zip` / `inventory-import.zip` — overwritten each run |\n| Timestamp applied | At archive/fail move time — not on upload |\n| Archive filename pattern | `{fixed-name}-{YYYYMMDD-HHmmss}.zip` e.g. `catalog-import-20250709-143022.zip` |\n| Archive on success | MuleSoft MOVE: `incoming/` → `archive/` with timestamp |\n| Archive on failure | MuleSoft MOVE: `incoming/` → `failed/` with timestamp + raise alert |\n| SFCC cleanup | SFCC does **not** clean up WebDAV files — MuleSoft owns full lifecycle |\n| Retention | Archive and failed folders purged on a rolling 30-day window — MuleSoft scheduled cleanup job |\n\n---\n\n8-sfcc-import-job-configuration8. SFCC Import Job Configuration\n---------------------------------------------------------------\n\nThe `sfcc-site-archive-import` system job is triggered by MuleSoft via the **SCAPI Jobs Admin API**. OCAPI is deprecated and must not be used for new integrations.\n\n| Aspect | Detail |\n| --- | --- |\n| Job ID | `sfcc-site-archive-import` |\n| API | SCAPI Jobs Admin API — `POST /jobs/v1/organizations/{organizationId}/jobs/{jobId}/executions` |\n| API reference | <https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/commerce/commerce-api/references/jobs> |\n| Auth | Account Manager OAuth2 (AmOAuth2) — client credentials grant. Registered in Account Manager, **not** in BM OCAPI settings |\n| Base URL | `https://{shortCode}.api.commercecloud.salesforce.com/jobs/v1/organizations/{organizationId}` |\n| Guard check | `GET .../jobs/sfcc-site-archive-import/executions?status=Running` — before every upload |\n| Job trigger | `POST .../jobs/sfcc-site-archive-import/executions` with `ImportFile` and `ImportMode` parameters |\n| Status poll | `GET .../jobs/sfcc-site-archive-import/executions/{executionId}` — poll until `executionStatus` ≠ `\"running\"` |\n| Success condition | `executionStatus: \"finished\"` + `exitStatus: \"ok\"` |\n| Failure condition | `executionStatus: \"finished\"` + `exitStatus: \"error\"`, or `executionStatus: \"failed\"` |\n| BM import log | `GET` from WebDAV `/Impex/log/` after job completion — required to detect per-record errors when job-level status is `ok` |\n| Job configuration | BM → Administration → Operations → Jobs |\n\n> **Important:** SFCC job status reflects job-level outcome only. A job can return `exitStatus: \"ok\"` while individual product or price records fail validation. MuleSoft **must** fetch and parse the BM import log after every successful job execution to detect partial failures.\n\n---\n\n9-error-handling9. Error Handling\n---------------------------------\n\n| Scenario | Handling |\n| --- | --- |\n| Previous job still running | SCAPI guard check before upload — hold and retry; do not overwrite `incoming/` until clear |\n| WebDAV upload failure | MuleSoft retries up to 3 times with 30-second interval; raises alert on persistent failure |\n| Job trigger failure (SCAPI error) | MuleSoft retries up to 3 times; raises alert — file remains in `incoming/` for manual replay |\n| Job exitStatus: error / failed | MuleSoft moves zip to `failed/` with timestamp; raises alert via Anypoint monitoring |\n| Job ok but log contains record errors | MuleSoft parses BM log; raises alert listing failed product/price/inventory IDs |\n| Corrupt or invalid XML | SFCC job fails immediately; MuleSoft catches via failed status; zip moved to `failed/` |\n| Archive folder full / WebDAV quota | Retention cleanup job prevents accumulation; monitored via Anypoint |\n\n---\n\n10-sync-flow-diagram10. Sync Flow Diagram\n-----------------------------------------\n\ncenterhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/whiteboard/315883522?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNGEyZTc4YTdlNzdhNGYwOTkyNDRiZjE2YWY4MjA2YzAiLCJwIjoiYyJ9false600\n\n11-open-items11. Open Items\n---------------------------\n\n| # | Item | Owner | Status |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Confirm product sync trigger pattern — event-driven on AP21 product change vs scheduled batch; confirm full vs delta feed scope | Integration Lead / MuleSoft team | Open |\n| 2 | Confirm price sync frequency — daily full reload vs delta on price change | Integration Lead / Zimmermann Finance | Open |\n| 3 | Confirm inventory sync region coverage for EU, EUIntl, HK, ME — current MuleSoft `inventory-sync-prc-api` covers AU, GB, US only | Integration Lead / Platform team | Open |\n| 4 | Confirm Account Manager OAuth2 client registration for MuleSoft — required for SCAPI Jobs Admin API and WebDAV access across sandbox, staging, and production | Integration Lead / SFCC Admin | Open |\n| 5 | Confirm WebDAV quota limits per environment and agree retention window for archive and failed folders | Integration Lead / SFCC Admin | Open |\n| 6 | Confirm whether MuleSoft log parsing (for per-record BM import errors) is in scope for MuleSoft team or SFCC team | Integration Lead / SFCC Lead | Open |",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "emoji": "1f504",
    "page_width": "fixed-width"
  }
}"}

