    "content": {
      "value": "Overview\n--------\n\nThe `zimmermann-sfcc-admin` GitHub repository contains automated workflows for provisioning SFCC (Salesforce Commerce Cloud) sandboxes. All provisioning is triggered manually via GitHub Actions `workflow_dispatch`.\n\n**Repository:**<https://github.com/ZimmermannAU/zimmermann-sfcc-admin>\n\n---\n\nWorkflow: Create Sandbox\n------------------------\n\n### How to Run\n\n1. Go to [GitHub Actions → Create Sandbox](https://github.com/ZimmermannAU/zimmermann-sfcc-admin/actions/workflows/sandbox-create.yml)\n2. Click **Run workflow**\n3. Fill in the inputs (see below)\n4. Click **Run workflow**\n\n---\n\nInputs\n------\n\n| Input | Required | Default | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **email** | Yes | — | Developer email address — used to grant BM Admin access |\n| **action** | Yes | `developer-sandbox` | Provisioning method (see below) |\n| **realm\\_id** | Yes | `bkzk` | SFCC Realm ID |\n| **profile** | Yes | `medium` | Resource profile: `medium`, `large`, `xlarge` |\n| **ttl** | Yes | `0` | Time-to-live in hours. `0` = realm default |\n| **schedule** | No | `business-hours-aest` | Auto start/stop schedule (developer-sandbox only) |\n\n---\n\nProvisioning Methods\n--------------------\n\n### `developer-sandbox` (default)\n\nCreates a **fresh blank sandbox** in the specified realm.\n\n* Applies OCAPI settings from `config/ocapi-settings.json`\n* Applies WebDAV permissions from `config/webdav-permissions.json`\n* Applies the selected auto-schedule\n* Grants the developer `bm-admin` (Business Manager Administrator) role\n\n**Schedules available:**\n\n| Option | Start | Stop | Days |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `business-hours-aest` | 8:00 AM AEST | 6:00 PM AEST | Mon–Fri |\n| `business-hours-aest-extended` | 7:00 AM AEST | 9:00 PM AEST | Mon–Fri |\n| `none` | — | — | Always on |\n\n---\n\n### `development-environment`\n\nClones the **DEV sandbox** (`d28e12d2-25f6-4937-9b9f-3c0610d01fd6`) to create a new sandbox with all DEV data, code, and configuration.\n\n* Calls the SFCC Sandbox REST API to initiate the clone\n* Polls until the clone is `COMPLETED` (up to 20 minutes)\n* Applies OCAPI and WebDAV settings to the new sandbox\n* Grants the developer `bm-admin` role\n\n---\n\nWhat Happens After Provisioning\n-------------------------------\n\n1. ✅ Sandbox created / cloned\n2. ✅ OCAPI settings applied (`config/ocapi-settings.json`)\n3. ✅ WebDAV permissions applied (`config/webdav-permissions.json`)\n4. ✅ Auto-schedule configured (developer-sandbox only)\n5. ✅ `bm-admin` role granted to the developer's email\n6. ✅ Workflow summary shows hostname and details\n\n---\n\nDeveloper Setup\n---------------\n\nOnce the workflow completes, the developer can find the sandbox hostname in the **workflow summary** under the Actions run.\n\n### dw.json\n\njson{\n\"hostname\": \"<sandbox-hostname>\",\n\"username\": \"<your-bm-username>\",\n\"password\": \"<your-bm-password>\",\n\"code-version\": \"version1\"\n}\n\n### .env\n\nnoneSFCC\\_HOSTNAME=<sandbox-hostname>\nSFCC\\_CLIENT\\_ID=<ask-your-team-lead>\nSFCC\\_CLIENT\\_SECRET=<ask-your-team-lead>\n> Credentials are stored securely as GitHub Actions secrets. Contact your team lead to obtain BM and API credentials.\n\n---\n\nRepository Structure\n--------------------\n\nnonezimmermann-sfcc-admin/\n├── .github/\n│ └── workflows/\n│ └── sandbox-create.yml # Main provisioning workflow\n├── config/\n│ ├── ocapi-settings.json # OCAPI client permissions\n│ └── webdav-permissions.json # WebDAV client permissions\n├── package.json # sfcc-ci dependency\n└── package-lock.json\n\n---\n\nGitHub Secrets Required\n-----------------------\n\n| Secret | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| `SFCC_CLIENT_ID` | API client ID for authentication |\n| `SFCC_CLIENT_SECRET` | API client secret for authentication |\n\nSet these under **GitHub → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions**.\n\n---\n\nTroubleshooting\n---------------\n\n| Error | Cause | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `Authentication failed` | Secrets not set or expired | Check `SFCC_CLIENT_ID` / `SFCC_CLIENT_SECRET` in repo secrets |\n| `Access is denied` | Client not assigned Sandbox API role for realm | Add client to realm in Account Manager |\n| `sandbox:realm:list` returns `[]` | No realm access | Grant Sandbox Administrator role on realm `bkzk` in Account Manager |\n| Clone times out | Large sandbox taking >20 min | Re-run — clone may have completed; check sandbox list |\n| `bm-admin` grant fails | User not in Account Manager | Ensure developer has an Account Manager account before running |",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "page_width": "fixed-width"
  }
}"}

