      "value": "purposePurpose\n--------------\n\nThis page is a **working document** used to define which Business Manager (BM) roles need to be configured in Salesforce Commerce Cloud (SFCC).\n\n---\n\ncontextContext\n--------------\n\nThe current Magento setup has **5 user roles**. The functional requirements do not explicitly define which roles are needed in SFCC BM. This workshop aims to:\n\n1. Identify all roles required in Business Manager\n2. Map permissions per role using the real BM permission structure\n3. Align with the personas defined in 04.3 Personas\n\n---\n\nmagento-roles-current-stateMagento Roles (Current State)\n--------------------------------------------------------\n\n> ⚠️ **To do:** Obtain this list from a Magento admin or business team\n\n| **#** | **Role Name** | **Description** | **Notes** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | *Administrators* |  | Incl. Digital Content |\n| 2 | *CS OP CRM Managers* |  |  |\n| 3 | *Content & Marketing* |  | Might rename this role? Studio & Marketing |\n| 4 | *Ops & Finance* |  |  |\n| 5 | *CS & CRM* |  |  |\n| 6 | *Lengow* |  | Not used anymore |\n\n![image-20260721-065704.png](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/rest/api/content/344883203/child/attachment/att346193940/download)\n\n---\n\nhow-sfcc-bm-roles-workHow SFCC BM Roles Work\n--------------------------------------------\n\nEach role in BM is configured across **7 permission tabs**. Permissions can be scoped to: - **Organisation** — applies across all sites - **Specific site(s)** — e.g. ZimmermannAU, ZimmermannEU, ZimmermannUK, ZimmermannUS, ZimmermannHK, ZimmermannME, ZimmermannEUIntl, ZimmermannUSIntl\n\n> 💡 This means roles can be **global** (org-scoped) or **regional** (site-scoped). A key workshop question is whether Zimmermann needs both — e.g. a Global Merchandiser vs an EU Merchandiser.\n\n---\n\nsfcc-bm-roles--working-draftSFCC BM Roles — Working Draft\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\n| **Role** | **Scope** | **Description** |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Administrator** | Organisation | Full access — already exists in sandbox. Overall org administration, users and roles. Security-sensitive. |\n| **Site Merchandiser** | Organisation | Manages products, categories, promotions, content and search. Could be global or per-region. |\n| **Client Services** | Organisation | View orders and customer accounts in BM. Can reset customer passwords. No order editing or on-behalf ordering. |\n| *(TBC — from Magento audit)* |  |  |\n| *(TBC — from Magento audit)* |  |  |\n\n---\n\nbm-permissions-matrixBM Permissions Matrix\n------------------------------------------\n\nPermissions in BM are organised across 6 categories (tabs). The matrix below uses these categories as rows — not individual permissions — with a description of what each covers and the access level per role.\n\n**Legend:** ✅ Full Access  |  🔶 Read Only  |  ✏️ Limited / Specific permissions  |  ❌ No Access  |  ⚠️ To be decided\n\n### business-manager-organisation-modulesBusiness Manager Organisation Modules\n\nThis lists the organisation context level BM permissions, which only the Administrator has access to.\n\n| **BM Module Group** | **What it covers** | **Administrator** |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Replication** | Data replication and code replication processes | ✅ |\n| **Organisation** | Org profile, Users, Roles & Permissions, Permission Audit, WebDAV Client Permissions | ✅ |\n| **Sites** | Manage Sites, Storefronts, Customer Lists, Content Libraries, Batch Processes, Embedded CDN | ✅ |\n| **Site Development** | Custom error/maintenance pages, Import & Export (site + dev), OCAPI Settings, Commerce API Settings | ✅ |\n| **Global Preferences** | Locales, Salesforce Connection, Timezone, Security, OAuth2, Pricing, Order Management config, Agentforce, Cross Cloud | ✅ |\n| **Operations** | Jobs, Job History, Import & Export Operations, GMV Reports, Custom Log Settings, Code/Pipeline Profiler, Custom Caches, Services, Change History, Encryption Keys | ✅ |\n\n### business-manager-sites-modulesBusiness Manager Sites Modules\n\nThese modules are site-scoped and represent the main workshop discussion. Permissions can be granted per individual site or across all sites.\n\n| **BM Module Group** | **What it covers** | **Administrator** | **Site Merchandiser** | **Client Services** | **TBD** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Products & Catalogs** | Products, Product List, Product Sets, Catalogs, Product Options, Visual Merchandising, Variation Attributes, Recommendations, Price Books, Import & Export Products | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ |  |\n| **Content** | Page Designer, Content Blocks, Libraries, Library Folders, Content Assets, Import & Export Content | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ |  |\n| **Search** | Search Indexes, Rebuild Schedule, Query Testing, Search Dictionaries (Stop Words, Synonyms, Hypernyms, Compound Words), Searchable Attributes, Search Driven Redirects, Search Suggestions | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ |  |\n| **AI & Social Integrations** | OpenAI configuration, Google web event tracking | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ |  |\n| **Online Marketing** | Campaigns, Promotions, A/B Tests, Content Slots, Coupons, Source Code Groups, Active Data, Stores, Gift Certificates, Import & Export Online Marketing, Consent Management, Notifications | ✅ | ✅ | ⚠️ (CS to give one time discount?) |  |\n| **Customers** | Customers, Customer Groups, Snapshots, Batch Processes Customers | ✅ | ⚠️ (what information does merchandising need to see here?) | 🔶 Customers (read + password reset if applicable) |  |\n| **Custom Objects** | Manage custom object definitions and instances for this site | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ |  |\n| **Ordering** | Orders, Commerce Apps, Taxation, Payment Processors, Payment Methods, Shipping Methods, Import & Export Ordering | ✅ | ❌ | 🔶 Orders (read only) |  |\n| **Analytics** | Reports & Dashboards, Historical BM Reports | ✅ | 🔶 | ⚠️(need?) |  |\n| **SEO & Discoverability** | URL Rules, URL Redirects, Static/Dynamic Mappings, Robots, Aliases, CDN Settings, Sitemaps, Page Meta Tag Rules | ✅ | ⚠️(need?) | ❌ |  |\n| **Site Preferences** | Locking, Baskets, Locales, Currencies, Coupon Preferences, Pricing & Promotions preferences, Storefront Login Preferences (incl. OTP config), Site Custom Preferences, Apple Pay | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ |  |\n| **AvaTax** | AvaTax Settings, Reconcile Orders, Exemption Certificates | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ |  |\n\n### functional-permissionsFunctional Permissions\n\nOrg-level functional permissions which are primarily assigned to the Administrator, and if applicable, to a global site merchandiser role.\n\n| **Permission** | **What it covers** | **Administrator** | **Site Merchandiser (content & marketing)** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Replication\\_Run\\_For\\_Org** | Start/manage global data replication | ✅ | ❌ |\n| **Granular\\_Replication\\_Publish\\_Objects** | Publish individual objects (e.g. products) to Production | ✅ | ❌ |\n| **Manage\\_All\\_Catalogs** | Manage all catalogs and assets across all sites | ✅ | ✅ |\n| **Delete\\_All\\_Catalogs** | Delete catalogs including all assets (prereq: Manage\\_All\\_Catalogs) | ✅ | ❌ |\n| **Manage\\_All\\_Libraries** | Manage all content libraries across all sites | ✅ | ✅ |\n| **Manage\\_All\\_PriceBooks** | Manage all pricebooks and product prices across all sites | ✅ | ✅ |\n| **Manage\\_Inventory** | Manage all inventory lists and records across all sites | ✅ | ✅ |\n| **Merge\\_Customers** | Merge customer records across customer lists | ✅ | ❌ |\n| **Manage\\_Users\\_Access\\_Keys** | Call Data API to manage users' access keys | ✅ | ❌ |\n| **Manage\\_Global\\_Sorting\\_Rules** | Create/edit/delete global sorting rules; promote site rules to global | ✅ | ✅ |\n| **View\\_Coupon\\_Codes** | Display full coupon codes in BM UI, OCAPI, and export | ✅ | ✅ |\n| **Modify\\_Beta\\_FeatureToggles** | Modify toggles for beta features | ✅ | ❌ |\n| **BM\\_Agentforce\\_Org** | Use Agentforce within Business Manager | ❌ | ❌ |\n\n### webdav-permissionsWebDAV Permissions\n\nFile system access via WebDAV. Typically only needed for technical/developer roles.\n\n| **Path** | **What it covers** | **Administrator** |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **/cartridges** | Access custom cartridge directories | ✅ |\n| **/realmdata** | Access realm-wide shared directory | ✅ |\n| **/securitylogs** | Access security logs | ✅ |\n| **/Logs/**\\* | All log files and subfolders | ✅ |\n| **/catalogs/**\\* | All catalog folders | ✅ |\n| **/libraries/**\\* | All content library folders | ✅ |\n| **/static, /temp** | Static and temp file access | ✅ |\n\n### locale-permissionsLocale Permissions\n\nControls which locales a role can read/write content in.\n\n| **Locale scope** | **Administrator** | **Site Merchandiser** |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| All locales (Read + Write) | ✅ | ⚠️ |\n| Site-specific locales only | — | ⚠️ Regional roles TBD |\n\n> 💡 Workshop decision needed: should regional roles (e.g. EU Merchandiser) be locked to specific locales?\n\n---\n\nkey-workshop-questionsKey Workshop Questions\n--------------------------------------------\n\n* What are the 6 existing Magento roles? → **Owner:** Magento Admin, **Due:** Before workshop\n\n  + There are current 5 roles in Magento - screenshot shared by Emma\n* Do we need **global roles** (org-scoped) AND **regional roles** (site-scoped)? e.g. Global Merchandiser + EU Merchandiser, CS AU / Global CS\n\n  + Currently - they are global. Would like the ability to have regional roles in the future.\n* Can Client Services continue to **create one-time promotions** for customers in SFCC?\n\n  + The consideration here is that there's no native cap in the promotions engine, so either a role has access to the entire Promotions engine or no access at all. Alternative option: CS doesn't get Promotions access in BM at go-live, and the rare Gold VIP coupon cases in HK/ME get handled by Merchandising on request. Or we could give CS access to coupon codes - they can generate a coupon code but the promotion against which it is generated needs to be set up by Merchandising. → real-time need probably, restriction would be inefficient\n  + This process is because give-x is not supported today in HK/ME - in the future state - we want this to work then CS won’t need to create promotions code\n  + Dani sees promotion codes also for UK/AU today - we need to check with Client Services why they’re creating these\n* Is there a need for a separate **Read-Only / Reporting** role (e.g. Finance, Management)?\n\n  + Finance has a role\n  + Management has a role - but elevated permissions\n  + Need workshops with the roles - to see if they need edit access or can fit into a read-only role for reporting/viewing\n* Who/what team is responsible for user management in Magento today? (if new employee joins, if someone needs additional permissions, etc.)\n\n  + This is Kim\n\ndecisionsDecisions\n------------------\n\n| **Decision** | **Outcome** | **Date** |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Customer Service Center (CSC) is out of scope. (This becomes a relevant feature if Order on Behalf of ever becomes scope for SFCC) |  |  |\n| Client Services accesses BM directly — view Orders + Customers, reset passwords only |  |  |\n| Agentforce is out of scope for now, no need to assign Agentforce permissions (This becomes a relevant feature if there is future scope for Agentforce) |  |  |\n\naction-itemsAction Items\n------------------------\n\n| **Action** | **Owner** | **Due Date** | **Status** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Schedule role-specific workshop | @Lucy Fu @Jasmijn Tsang |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |\n\n---\n\nrelated-pagesRelated Pages\n--------------------------\n\n* 04.3 Personas",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
