      "value": "Overview\n--------\n\neCDN, WAF, and security configuration in BM protects Zimmermann's storefronts and controls CDN caching behaviour. Two significant platform-level changes are relevant for a new SFCC build: the migration from WAFv1 to WAFv2, and the disabling of the deprecated Storefront Toolkit. Both have security implications if left unconfigured.\n\n**📎 Salesforce Docs:** [eCDN Configuration in Business Manager](https://documentation.b2c.commercecloud.salesforce.com/DOC2/topic/com.demandware.dochelp/CDN/CDNConfiguration.html)  \n**📎 Salesforce Docs:** [Log Center Overview](https://documentation.b2c.commercecloud.salesforce.com/DOC2/topic/com.demandware.dochelp/OperationalInsights/LogCenter.html)  \n**📎 Salesforce Docs:** [B2C Commerce 25.7 Release Notes — Storefront Toolkit](https://documentation.b2c.commercecloud.salesforce.com/DOC2/topic/com.demandware.dochelp/ReleaseNotes/ReleaseNotes25_7.html)  \n**📎 Accenture Observability Deck:** See the Observability, Tracing & Security Assurance deck in this space for the shared responsibility model.\n\n**⚠️ Platform change (July 2025, v25.7):** The deprecated Storefront Toolkit is now **disabled by default** on all new and imported sites. If it was inadvertently re-enabled, disable it immediately.\n\n---\n\nChecklist\n---------\n\n### ~~eCDN & WAF Configuration~~\n\n1\nb43bcd559bae\nincomplete\n~~eCDN WAFv2 configured — confirm not still on legacy WAFv1 (self-service migration available in BM)~~\n\n2\nc669241cca08\nincomplete\n~~CDN zone configured for each production storefront domain~~\n\n3\n422c54288c5e\nincomplete\nCustom hostnames registered with eCDN-managed TLS certificates (auto-renewing)\n\n4\n83bc395f3005\nincomplete\nProduction instances are **not** using `demandware.net` or hyphenated hostnames for public traffic — vanity hostname must be used\n\n5\n130ea0a12f5a\nincomplete\nProxy zone created in staging instances if needed (for eCDN certificate management)\n\n### ~~Storefront Toolkit~~\n\n6\n7c84322b9fa6\nincomplete\nDeprecated Storefront Toolkit is **disabled** on all sites (v25.7 default — verify it has not been re-enabled)\n\n7\n12961afde075\nincomplete\nConfirmed no storefront code depends on the deprecated toolkit\n\n### ~~Security Headers (Accenture-configured — verify BM alignment)~~\n\n8\nac3d5244a044\nincomplete\nContent Security Policy (CSP) directives in BM align with Accenture's Helmet configuration\n\n9\n9893911136a5\nincomplete\nHSTS (HTTP Strict Transport Security) enabled\n\n10\n9daec868af16\nincomplete\nX-Frame-Options configured\n\n11\n8763e9d1dc6a\nincomplete\nReferrer-Policy configured\n\n### Log Centre Configuration\n\n12\n3d56cf354388\ncomplete\nLog Centre accessible in BM (Administration → Operations → Log Center)\n\n13\n359e9ae0fdc5\nincomplete\nLog Centre Streaming configured to route to the APM destination (New Relic — as recommended in the Observability deck)\n\n14\n1a2329551e04\nincomplete\nMRT request logs, error logs, and CDN logs confirmed streaming\n\n15\nacde6f14df2e\nincomplete\nSLAS error logs confirmed available in Log Centre\n\n### SCAPI Caching\n\n16\nba886fb95538\nincomplete\nSCAPI server-side web-tier caching is enabled (enabled by default for new zones provisioned after March 2024)\n\n17\nc337ab363602\nincomplete\nSCAPI caching tested — confirm cached responses are correct and not serving wrong-locale content\n\n### Penetration Testing (Zimmermann responsibility)\n\n18\n1c66de13a061\nincomplete\nThird-party application-layer pen test scoped and vendor procured\n\n19\nbadccd097e86\nincomplete\nPen test scope includes: PWA Kit application, SCAPI integration points, SLAS auth flows, custom API endpoints\n\n20\n664a3bb62fa6\nincomplete\nPen test scheduled post-UAT, pre go-live\n\n21\n58153b4ece13\nincomplete\nRepeat pen test planned 6 months post-launch\n\n---\n\nNotes / Findings\n----------------\n\n*Record gaps, decisions, and owner for remediation here.*\n\n| Finding | Severity | Owner | Resolved |\n| --- | ---